     zzffss hhoolldd [--rr] _t_a_g _s_n_a_p_s_h_o_tâ¦
       Adds a single reference, named with the _t_a_g argument, to the specified
       snapshots.  Each snapshot has its own tag namespace, and tags must be
       unique within that space.

       If a hold exists on a snapshot, attempts to destroy that snapshot by
       using the zzffss ddeessttrrooyy command return EEBBUUSSYY.

       --rr  Specifies that a hold with the given tag is applied recursively to
           the snapshots of all descendent file systems.

     zzffss hhoollddss [--rrHHpp] _s_n_a_p_s_h_o_tâ¦
       Lists all existing user references for the given snapshot or snapshots.

       --rr  Lists the holds that are set on the named descendent snapshots, in
           addition to listing the holds on the named snapshot.

       --HH  Do not print headers, use tab-delimited output.

       --pp  Prints holds timestamps as unix epoch timestamps.

     zzffss rreelleeaassee [--rr] _t_a_g _s_n_a_p_s_h_o_tâ¦
       Removes a single reference, named with the _t_a_g argument, from the spec‐
       ified snapshot or snapshots.  The tag must already exist for each snap‐
       shot.  If a hold exists on a snapshot, attempts to destroy that snap‐
       shot by using the zzffss ddeessttrrooyy command return EEBBUUSSYY.

       --rr  Recursively releases a hold with the given tag on the snapshots of
           all descendent file systems.

